    "title": "2. Where Smart Money comes from and who they are",
    "summary": "The Smart Money idea comes from the stock market, not from crypto.",
    "content": "The Smart Money idea comes from the stock market, not from crypto.\n\n\n### Why the stock market\nThe volume of the stock market is extremely high compared with crypto.\n\nThere is also algorithmic trading that moves the price in the direction the big players want.\n\nThis lets institutional traders, banks and hedge funds build their positions in the best price range.\n\n\n### Who is \"Smart Money\"?\nInstitutional traders, banks, hedge funds, and any trader with a huge portfolio.\n\nThey have far larger amounts to trade with than a normal person.\n\n\n### Why it is now used in crypto\nThe concept has been used for a long time in the stock market, with algorithms.\n\nCrypto is now getting huge volumes too, so it is becoming more like the stock market.\n\nThat is why Smart Money Concepts also work on crypto charts. Roman and the host use Bitcoin charts in the lesson.\n\nIt is also not only about crypto: the same ideas apply in the stock market and in Forex.\n\n\n### A very old idea\nRoman says this idea is similar to what a trader named Richard Wyckoff described about 100 years ago, long before Bitcoin. Smart Money is a simpler version of it. See Section 8.",
