    "id": "ch1-sec3",
    "num": "03",
    "title": "3. Smart Money vs retail traders",
    "summary": "The big difference is size: Smart Money is so large that it needs many small traders on the other side of every order.",
    "content": "The big difference is size: Smart Money is so large that it needs many small traders on the other side of every order.\n\n\n| Category | Smart Money (institutions) | Retail traders |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Who | Banks, hedge funds, traders with huge portfolios | Individual traders with small accounts |\n| Order size | Very large (for example, billions of dollars) | Small |\n| Main problem | They need other traders on the opposite side to fill their position | They are the other side |\n| How they enter | Slowly, with algorithms, in many small parts | One order at a time, often at obvious levels |\n| What they use | Liquidity, market structure, order flow | Indicators, support and resistance |\n| Relation to liquidity | They move the price into levels of high liquidity | They put stop losses just below swing lows or above swing highs |\n\n\n### The $10 billion example\nRoman asks: what if you want to buy Bitcoin worth 10 billion dollars?\n\nYou need enough retail traders to sell into that much money.\n\nYou cannot do it in one order. A single market order for that size would push the price very high, and you would buy at terrible prices.\n\nSo Smart Money uses algorithms. First they move the price down.\n\nThen they slowly fill small parts of their position, until they are ready.\n\nThen they move the price up. That is where they make their profit.\n\nThe other direction works the same way. When Smart Money wants to sell, it moves the price up to where retail traders are buying, and sells to them.\n\n\n### Our goal as retail traders\nGet in where they get in, so we ride the wave with them when they push the price up.\n\nBecause their orders are so big, they cannot fill them without leaving clues. If we know what to look for, we can notice those clues on the chart.\n\nThat is the reason to learn this concept: it helps you find the clues and move in the same direction as Smart Money.\n\n\n### How a big order is filled",
