    "id": "ch1-sec6",
    "num": "06",
    "title": "6. Manipulation tactic 1: the stop hunt and the cascade",
    "summary": "A stop hunt pushes the price into a level full of stop losses, and each triggered stop pushes the price further, like a chain reaction.",
    "content": "A stop hunt pushes the price into a level full of stop losses, and each triggered stop pushes the price further, like a chain reaction.\n\n\n### How the cascade works, step by step\nPrice reaches the area just below a swing low.\n\nThe first stop losses are triggered. They are sell orders.\n\nThese sells push the price further down.\n\nPrice reaches the next group of sell orders. They trigger too, and push the price even lower.\n\nThis repeats, again and again. The host explains how it works on an exchange: a stop loss becomes a market order when triggered. It clears the order book, then the next one is triggered, then the next. You get a big waterfall of orders.\n\nThis liquidity was hidden. It was not in the order book before. Now it suddenly becomes available.\n\nWhile these sell orders are being filled, the large traders buy. They are the other side of all those sells.\n\nAfter that, they move the price up.\n\n\n### Why Smart Money wants this\nThis is exactly what they look for: lots of volume available at a good price. For us, it is a clear sign that the price is about to be pushed up.\n\n\n### How it looks on a chart\nBig wicks, sometimes very big ones, are usually caused by stop losses being triggered in a chain.\n\nA typical shape is a hammer candle: a very small body with a very long wick pointing down.\n\n\n### A real example from the lesson (a stop hunt on an uptrend)\nThe chart is going up with a clear pattern of higher highs and higher lows. A trader sees a swing low as a good support.\n\nThe trader enters near it, puts the stop loss below the recent swing low, and sets the take profit higher.\n\nFirst, one wick goes down. It does not go below the swing low, so the trade is still alive.\n\nThen price drops below the swing low. The trader is stopped out. A lot of sell orders are executed.\n\nAt this moment, the breakout traders also start selling. They open new short positions as soon as price breaks the level. Their sells add to the cascade.\n\nThe price keeps falling in this chain of orders.\n\nThen it turns, and the price goes up. Smart Money has taken the liquidity and starts to push the price up.\n\n\n### The cascade in a drawing",
