    "id": "ch1-sec8",
    "num": "08",
    "title": "8. Wyckoff, psychology and real-world manipulation",
    "summary": "The tricks Smart Money uses are old: the market is mostly psychology, and a trader named Wyckoff described this about 100 years ago.",
    "content": "The tricks Smart Money uses are old: the market is mostly psychology, and a trader named Wyckoff described this about 100 years ago.\n\n\n### Who was Richard Wyckoff?\nA trader who wrote many documents and strategies on trading. The host had heard of him, and Roman explained him to the viewers.\n\nHis main discovery: everything in the market is psychology.\n\nIf you make the chart look like a certain pattern, you create the best psychology to make retail traders panic or get greedy.\n\nSmart Money Concepts are a simpler version of what Wyckoff said.\n\n\n### The Wyckoff distribution (how the trap works)\nPush the price up in a specific pattern.\n\nMake it look like there will be a small correction, followed by a big move up. Retail traders buy.\n\nThen \"nope\": push the price all the way down. Smart Money was selling to those buyers on the way.\n\nRoman says a pattern like this appeared in Bitcoin a couple of years before the stream. In his view, it pushed the price down to the area of 20,000 and 16,000 in the last bear market, as a clear case of manipulation so big players could get in at low prices. He says the same thing happens on smaller time frames and smaller moves.\n\n\n### What Smart Money does outside the chart\n\n### A viewer asked: to push the price down, don't they have to sell some Bitcoin first? Answer: yes, they do. But on a larger scale they do more\nThey sell Bitcoin first to push the price down.\n\nThey can create market sentiment outside the market: push news items, create FOMO, create fear.\n\nSometimes they open a losing position on purpose to move the price. When the price reaches the range where they want to buy, they make back all those losses.\n\nSo their investment is not just the coins they buy. It is the whole thing around it.\n\n\n### What the hosts say about recent Bitcoin\nThey observed that Bitcoin was trading in a pattern with very strange daily candles: open and close almost the same, with a high and low only about 2.5% apart.\n\nTheir view: either big players are accumulating, or they are slowly selling to keep the price down before another push. They say they do not know for sure, but they believe there was manipulation.\n\nPlease read these claims with care. These are the opinions of the two presenters. Treat them as a model that explains price moves, not as proven facts.\n\nA viewer also mentioned ICT, a well-known teacher of Smart Money ideas. The hosts said they are not following ICT. They follow traders who share their setups live, and they only try to interpret and learn the ideas themselves.\n\n\n### The Wyckoff idea in a drawing",
