    "id": "ch1-sec9",
    "num": "09",
    "title": "9. A real chart example: sweep, shift, retest, entry",
    "summary": "The most basic Smart Money entry is: price sweeps a liquidity level, the structure shifts on a lower time frame, and you enter after the retest.",
    "content": "The most basic Smart Money entry is: price sweeps a liquidity level, the structure shifts on a lower time frame, and you enter after the retest.\n\n\n### Step by step (a long example)\nOn the daily chart, a swing low is a point of interest (POI). Price comes down into it.\n\nPrice sweeps the liquidity below the swing low. A lot of stop losses are triggered.\n\nBecause the daily chart moves slowly, you switch to a lower time frame (here, 1 hour).\n\nOn the 1-hour chart you see the smart money reversal pattern: a liquidity sweep first.\n\nThen the structure breaks: price breaks the last lower high. This is the shift in market structure.\n\nYou enter as soon as price breaks that lower high and retests it.\n\nRoman calls this the most basic Smart Money reversal setup. As soon as you see this shift in structure, it suggests that the market is ready to move in the new direction.\n\n\n### Where price goes next\nThe target is the next level of liquidity. In the lesson, price went there and took out the short traders whose stop losses were around a swing high.\n\nRoman says the target could also be a fair value gap area, or even lower, to a liquidity zone.\n\nFor the stop loss, the example in Chapter 2 places it beyond the sweep.\n\n\n### The result\nThe position had a risk-to-reward ratio of about 6.5. The host says it was about a 49% move.\n\nIf you risk 1% of your portfolio, this trade gains about 6.5% of your portfolio.\n\nIf you risk 5%, it gains about 30%. The host adds: that is a massive move.\n\nRoman says he once had a month with about 70% growth on his futures account, and about 40% in another month, but it is not consistent yet. That is why he chooses the learning path.\n\nA reminder from both presenters: they are not experts. They do not tell you to risk your money or say you will become rich.\n\n\n### Volume and RSI: extra confirmation only\nIn Smart Money, volume is not an indicator to trade with. It is extra confirmation.\n\nIt is useful when price is consolidating in a range, to understand where you are in the market.\n\nYou can also use RSI. When you see a possible reversal on the chart, look at the volume: if volume is increasing, it is another point for the reversal. Then look for divergence on the RSI. That is a third confirmation.\n\nMore confirmations give you a better decision.\n\n\n### The entry model in a drawing",
