    "title": "14. Homework, next lesson and honest warnings",
    "summary": "This lesson is the overview, so the real practice starts in the next lesson.",
    "content": "This lesson is the overview, so the real practice starts in the next lesson. You can still prepare now.\n\n\n### Suggested practice (my suggestion, not from the stream)\nOpen a chart of any market and mark the swing highs and swing lows as best you can.\n\nWrite a small note above each swing high (\"buy orders above\") and below each swing low (\"sell orders below\").\n\nLook for places where price swept a level with a wick and then reversed.\n\nPractise on old charts only. Place no trades.\n\nLearn the words in Section 15 until you can explain each one in your own words.\n\n\n### What comes next in the series\nNext lesson: how to properly identify the swing points. Roman learned that not every swing point is a proper, structural one. He would, for example, mark a point as a swing that is not one.\n\nAfter that: how to identify market structure, whether it is bullish or bearish, and how not to miss it. Roman says that knowing the direction in which Smart Money moves the market is the key to success. If you trade the wrong direction, you will be stopped out, even if your point of interest is right.\n\nYou will learn to draw higher highs and higher lows, and to know when a higher high is really a higher high and not part of internal price movement.\n\nThe series will also include exercises with the replay mode: drawing highs and lows, fair value gaps and order blocks. The hosts say it is tedious but necessary.\n\nOrder blocks, breaker blocks and more details on entries come later. Paper trading comes first, and live trading later.\n\nThe hosts say they may add an automatic fair value gap indicator to their tool in the future.\n\n\n### Honest warnings\nThe presenters are not experts. They are learning and sharing what they learned in a few weeks.\n\nNobody should risk money based only on this lesson. High leverage can wipe out an account very fast.\n\nThe profit numbers mentioned in the stream (for example a 70% month) come from one person's account, and he says himself that it is not consistent yet.\n\nThe claims about big players manipulating the market are the presenters' views and are not proven here.\n\nThese are study notes, not financial advice. I am not a financial advisor, so make your own decisions and think about your own risk.",
